## # Alya Multi-Precision Integer Library
##
## Part of the Alya Language package ecosystem (https://github.com/alya-lang).
## Unsigned big integers as little-endian `limb_bits()`-wide limb arrays.
## Powers RSA, ECDSA, and Diffie-Hellman in the `crypto` package.
##
## ```alya
## import "math" as math
##
## function main()
##     let p = math::bi_from_bytes([1, 2, 3])
##     let q = math::bi_from_bytes([4, 5, 6])
##     say math::bi_cmp(math::bi_add(p, q), p) # 1
## end
## ```

import "./bigint.alya"
import "./numtheory.alya"
import "./primes.alya"
import "./combin.alya"
import "./rational.alya"
import "./complex.alya"
import "./matrix.alya"
import "./poly.alya"

## Limb width in bits for the `bi_*` representation contract.
##
## Every limb holds a value below `2^limb_bits()`, little-endian first.
## Products of two limbs stay below 2^60, so every intermediate is exact
## in 64-bit signed arithmetic.
##
## NOTE: exposed as a function because an aliased `pub let` miscompiles
## (reads zero/garbage, see alya-lang/alya#48). Revisit when fixed.
pub function limb_bits() -> int
    return 30
end
